vLLM PR #54530 (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/54530, open), ported to v0.32.0 by hand: under priority
scheduling, when the running queue is full (max_num_seqs; max_num_active_reqs in 0.32.0), a waiting request may preempt
the lowest-priority running request if it has a strictly higher priority. The PR targets a newer main, whose waiting
loop differs. The closure takes back what the victim was scheduled in the step, as the running loop's preemption does.
The logger line keeps the scheduler's logger in the generated module, whose own name vLLM's logging config does not
cover.

